PREAMBLE
===============================================================================

The Sirdata mobile consent management SDK, including its object code, the
source files distributed with it, its documentation and accompanying
materials (together, the "Software"), is the property of Sirdata SAS, a
French societe par actions simplifiee ("Sirdata"). The Software is protected
by copyright and by the rights of the producer of a database where
applicable. The Software is licensed, not sold. Sirdata retains all rights
not expressly granted.

Sirdata publishes the Software on public package registries, including Maven
Central, CocoaPods, npm and the Swift Package Manager. Publication makes the
published artefacts publicly accessible; Sirdata makes no claim that those
published artefacts are secret or confidential, and this Licence imposes no
confidentiality obligation on them.

Publication does not transfer ownership and does not make the Software open
source. Nothing in this Preamble waives Sirdata's rights under Sections 2, 3
and 4.

Sirdata does claim, and takes reasonable steps to protect as trade secrets
within the meaning of Articles L. 151-1 et seq. of the French Commercial
Code, elements that are not published, including: server-side algorithms,
scoring and vendor-resolution logic; restricted integration, architecture and
support documentation made available under access control; API keys,
credentials and endpoint configuration; customer configuration data;
commercial terms; and product roadmap and unreleased developments (together,
the "Sirdata Protected and Confidential Elements", as defined in Section 4).
Those elements are disclosed only under access control or under a separate
agreement, and remain subject to Section 4.


