10. TERM, TERMINATION AND SURVIVAL
===============================================================================

10.1 Termination for breach. Either Party may terminate this Licence if the
other materially breaches it and fails to remedy the breach within thirty
(30) days of a written notice identifying the breach. Immediate termination
on written notice is available only for breach of Section 2 (Embedded
Distribution), Section 4 (Use of Sirdata Protected and Confidential
Elements), or unauthorised redistribution of the Software as a standalone
product.

10.2 Ordinary termination. Where the Software is supplied under a separate
subscription agreement, this Licence ends when that subscription ends, in
accordance with its own notice provisions. No automatic termination occurs
without notice.

10.3 Residual licence for distributed copies. Sirdata grants You and Your end
users a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free licence to continue
running the copies of the Software already embedded in application versions
distributed to end users before termination. This residual licence is limited
to continued operation and to the corrective maintenance of those versions.
It does not authorise new features, new integrations, or new server
entitlements.

10.4 Sell-off period. Application versions submitted to an application store
for review before termination may complete review and be released, and remain
covered by Section 10.3.

10.5 No new distribution. After termination You must not publish any new
application or new application version embedding the Software, except as
permitted by Section 10.4, and must remove the Software from Your development
and build environments.

10.6 Continuity of end-user rights. The Parties acknowledge that end users
must remain able to exercise their rights under Regulation (EU) 2016/679,
including withdrawal of consent under Article 7(3), through the consent
interface. For twelve (12) months from termination, Sirdata will continue to
operate the minimum backend services required for consent display, consent
withdrawal and signal storage for copies covered by Section 10.3, without
charge. Before the end of that period, You must either migrate the affected
application versions to another consent management solution or withdraw them
from distribution. This Section does not apply where termination results from
Your breach of Section 4, in which case Sirdata will nevertheless maintain
withdrawal functionality for six (6) months.

10.7 Survival. Sections 4, 6, 8.4, 9, 10.3 to 10.7, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 17,
18, 20, 24 and 26, and the Preamble, survive termination.


