14.2 Data processing agreement. Before any use of the Software in production,
the parties shall enter into a written data processing agreement ("DPA")
meeting the requirements of Article 28(3) GDPR. In respect of personal data,
the DPA prevails over this Licence to the extent of any inconsistency. In the
absence of an executed DPA, the Licensee shall not process the personal data
of natural persons through the Software in production. This restriction bears
on production processing only: integration and testing against an actual
Console configuration remain permitted under Sections 1.4 and 25.1.

14.3 Minimum content of the DPA. The DPA shall specify at least:
(a) the subject matter, nature, purpose and duration of the processing;
(b) the categories of data subjects and the types of personal data
    processed;
(c) the documented instructions of the controller, and the obligation for
    Sirdata to inform the Licensee where an instruction infringes applicable
    data protection law;
(d) the confidentiality undertakings of persons authorised to process the
    data;
(e) the technical and organisational security measures implemented pursuant
    to Article 32 GDPR;
(f) the conditions for engaging sub-processors, the list of approved
    sub-processors and the procedure for notifying changes together with the
    Licensee's right to object;
(g) the assistance provided to the Licensee in responding to data subject
    requests under Chapter III GDPR;
(h) the assistance provided to the Licensee in respect of Articles 32 to 36
    GDPR, including personal data breach notification without undue delay;
(i) the arrangements for deletion or return of the personal data at the end
    of the provision of services, and for deletion of existing copies unless
    retention is required by Union or Member State law;
(j) the arrangements for making available the information necessary to
    demonstrate compliance with Article 28 GDPR and for allowing and
    contributing to audits, and the conditions governing any transfer of
    personal data to a third country, including the applicable transfer
    mechanism.

14.4 Local storage. The Software writes and reads consent signals and related
technical parameters in the storage of the end user's terminal equipment. The
Licensee is solely responsible for ensuring that the storing of, and access
to, such information complies with Article 5(3) of Directive 2002/58/EC as
transposed in each jurisdiction where its applications are made available,
