specification and the IAB Global Privacy Platform. The Licensee's use of the
Software does not of itself confer on the Licensee any registration,
certification, validation or membership status under those frameworks. The
Licensee remains responsible for obtaining and maintaining any status,
registration or authorisation required by the relevant framework operator.

15.2 Licensee undertakings. The Licensee undertakes:
(a) to configure and operate the Software in accordance with the applicable
    framework policies, technical specifications and the terms of use of the
    relevant framework operator;
(b) not to alter, suppress, forge, pre-populate, override or otherwise
    manipulate any consent signal, string or transparency disclosure produced
    by the Software in a manner inconsistent with those policies or with
    applicable law;
(c) not to represent that a consent signal reflects a user choice that was
    not in fact expressed by that user;
(d) to maintain the integrity of the vendor list, purpose, special purpose,
    feature and special feature disclosures as delivered by the Software,
    save for configuration options expressly exposed by the Software;
(e) to notify Sirdata without undue delay of any notice, complaint, audit
    request or enforcement action received from a framework operator, an
    industry body or a supervisory authority in connection with the Software.

15.3 Suspension. Where the Licensee is in breach of Section 15.2, Sirdata may
suspend the Licensee's access to the Software and to any related remote
service after giving ten (10) working days' prior notice to remedy the
breach. No prior notice is required where the breach is manifest or
continuing, or where immediate suspension is required by a framework
operator, a supervisory authority or applicable law.

15.4 Framework changes. Framework policies and specifications are defined and
amended by their respective operators and are outside Sirdata's control.
Sirdata may modify the Software to reflect such changes. Sirdata gives no
