request a written self-certification signed by an authorised representative
of the Licensee. The Licensee shall return that self-certification within
thirty (30) days of the request. A complete and accurate self-certification
discharges the Licensee for the period covered.

19.3 Costs. Each party bears its own costs. Where the verification reveals an
under-declaration or a non-compliant use exceeding five percent (5%) of the
declared scope, the Licensee shall bear the reasonable costs of the
verification and shall regularise its position, including by paying any
additional fees due, within thirty (30) days.

19.4 Confidentiality. Information obtained in the course of a verification is
confidential, shall be used solely to assess compliance with this Licence and
to enforce Sirdata's rights, and shall not be disclosed to third parties
other than Sirdata's advisers bound by an equivalent duty of confidentiality.


