25. PRECEDENCE AND UPGRADE
===============================================================================

25.1 What entitles you to production use. Production use — meaning any use of
the Software in an application distributed, published or otherwise made
available to end users, whether or not for consideration — requires a valid
and current subscription to the Sirdata Consent Management Platform, and is
governed by Section 1.3. A subscription taken through the Sirdata Console is
sufficient: no separately signed commercial agreement is required. Where you
hold no such subscription, your rights are those of the evaluation grant in
Section 1.4 — internal evaluation, development, testing and integration, with
no distribution to any third party or public application store. Nothing in
this Section restricts the use of real configuration data during evaluation:
a consent management platform can only be integrated against an actual
configuration. Subscriptions: https://sirdata.com — questions:
legal@sirdata.com.

25.2 Precedence. A separately signed commercial agreement is optional and is
not a condition of production use. Where such an agreement is nevertheless in
place and covers the Software, it prevails over this Licence to the extent of
any inconsistency. The following provisions of this Licence nevertheless
continue to apply and are not displaced unless the signed agreement expressly
states otherwise by reference to the relevant section: Section 12 (Ownership),
Section 6 (Third-Party Components) and Section 13 (Language). In respect of
personal data, the data processing agreement prevails in accordance with
Section 14.2.

25.3 Automatic upgrade. Where the parties execute a commercial agreement
covering the Software after the Licensee has begun using it under this
Licence, that agreement applies from its effective date to all use of the
Software, including use of copies obtained before that date, unless the
agreement provides otherwise.

25.4 Reversion. On expiry or termination of your subscription, or of any
signed commercial agreement, without renewal, your rights revert to the
evaluation grant in Section 1.4 and production use shall cease for new
releases, subject to Section 10.3 (residual licence for copies already
distributed), Section 10.4 (sell-off) and Section 10.6 (continuity of
end-user rights).


